  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed extension of the vehicular access road, by reason of its siting, design and materials proposed, would result in the loss of existing green space at the end of the cul-de-sac and introduce a visually intrusive and incongruous feature into the street scene. The surfacing is unlikely to remain attractive under regular vehicular use, leading to a poor-quality appearance. The development would therefore harm the character and appearance of the area and disrupt the established form of the existing cul-de-sac. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies D3 and D4 of the  London Plan (2021) Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policy DMD 37 of the Development Management Document (2014)and Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).",
    "In the absence of a clear and detailed plan showing the proposed parking layout and vehicle manoeuvring at the end of the access road, it is not possible to determine whether the arrangement would operate safely or efficiently, potentially resulting in protracted and complex vehicle manoeuvres which would have an adverse impact on the residential amenity of existing occupiers through additional noise and general disturbance. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan (2021) Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD 8 and DMD 37 of the Development Management Document (2014) and Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024)."
  ],
